  "declaredIdentity": "Tenant / audit-populations / populationId (Define handler uses DefinitionId); definition/source/row/export identities checked; one shared expectedRevision; several mutators check revision before retry. Portia appends against the hydrated physical stream position; a logical revision does not create another physical boundary.",
  "invariant": "One population owns complete current definition/source/row classification, reconciliation invalidation, completeness proof and freeze seal. Immutable row/version bodies are values outside retained command state; no independent AuditPopulationRowDecision root or projected-count freeze authority.",
  "boundaryDecision": "narrow",
  "boundaryRationale": "Keep current complete row/category/source reconciliation and authoritative freeze seal together. Immutable row/version content may use chunked capsules and history projections; independent export attempts need their own process/identity. No per-row projected counts may decide freeze.",
